      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The shift to electronic warfare fundamentally changes the nature of maritime dominance by moving the battlefield from visible, kinetic power to invisible, informational control. Where the Great Khan's fleets relied on sheer size and visible martial might, modern dominance is achieved by controlling the electromagnetic spectrum, effectively blinding or deafening adversaries. This means that the ability to jam communications or spoof navigation systems is now as crucial as the strength of the hull.",
      "source": "target",
